#: ../../reference/files.rst:2 16d7a907fe7d4152b32a44c56ea6f559
msgid "Files, printing and packaging"
msgstr "File, stampa e pacchettizzazione"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:7 da8a21da5bf141d2a1ded82e8ffe9b87
msgid "Storage"
msgstr "Archiviazione"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:9 0bed7e7e6eee4b21933c443b99cb6f3f
msgid ""
"One folder per competition. Everything the jury makes is in it, and it "
"copies to a memory stick at the end of the day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:27 207ac375db1144e0995aa57eb16bc48a
msgid ""
"The root is ``competitions/`` in a checkout and ``Documents\\BlueBand`` "
"when installed, overridden by ``COMMISSAIRE_TRACK_DATA`` either way. "
"Competition folders are the jury's work and stay out of the repository — "
"the one exception is ``competitions/example/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:33 63437a1d467c429ba44db9a0bd7805bb
msgid "Nothing is lost"
msgstr "Niente si perde"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:35 decf5c2b05d24462a9a260cdf287f148
msgid ""
"Every write is atomic — temp file plus ``os.replace`` — and keeps the "
"previous content as a snapshot. Nothing typed by the jury can be lost by "
"a crash, a bad edit or a browser reload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:47 2833dfbe36754c38881be35fd84597ce
msgid ""
"``journal.jsonl`` is append-only and never rewritten: one line per write,"
" with the action, the target and the time. It is what answers *what "
"happened at 14:30* — including why a PDF came out as HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:51 43058c2499d14b7999d6fa3311dbf607
msgid ""
"``races/<race_id>.json`` is a ``RaceState``, and everything a format "
"needs lives in its ``payload``. The race id is ``race.race_key(cat, "
"event, round_key)``, and round keys are the strings written in "
"``programme.yaml`` — which is why translating a round name would orphan "
"its race file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:56 c4111379a8dc4e60a3a08195572822aa
msgid ""
"``settings.json`` holds the choices of *this machine and this "
"competition*: ``language``, ``out_dir``, ``use_overlay``, the letterhead "
"in progress, and various UI keys. Anything that is a statement about the "
"**competition** — what a team is, the entry-file layout, the branding — "
"lives in ``programme.yaml``, not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:63 b2055f7abda1449eb4051b2340f47249
msgid "``core.paths``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:65 4e07f410d08e4ffbbf32a263479466df
msgid ""
"Run from the repository, every path answers with the repository. "
"Installed, two different places, and conflating them is how a jury loses "
"a championship."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:68 4b555b5884da469fbb83ff9daacccdae
msgid "``bundle()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:69 160a7a7d8b5b45878ae76093619dbdcd
msgid ""
"**What the program is** — regulations, templates, stylesheet. Read-only, "
"replaced wholesale by the next version, and under PyInstaller it lives in"
" ``sys._MEIPASS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:73 b603c409fcc24d12ae7b423acfd4a98f
msgid "``data()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:74 652dfcb462884bb2b84c8a42ff250667
msgid ""
"**What the jury made** — competitions, results, communiqués. It must "
"outlive an uninstall, be findable without a file manager, and be easy to "
"copy to a stick, so it goes in the user's Documents and never inside the "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:78 4fe0052fda0f4ef4af664497fe0a8930
msgid "``served()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:79 26143d55cf744cc282c6ccfc72bea120
msgid ""
"The copies of the last saved PDFs that Streamlit serves out of "
"``static/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:81 4da4b7c1c79642ad8653866ab302b808
msgid ""
"``core.paths`` is the only module that knows any of this, which is why "
"nothing else in the codebase had to learn about ``sys._MEIPASS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:88 c359c3c819a4418a9543912f38095915
msgid "Regulation files"
msgstr "I file del regolamento"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:90 5b5de1caaabf4f5cbf64680408735b11
msgid ""
"Eight JSON tables under ``regulations/``. **The regulation is data, not "
"code**: a rule that changes next year is a file edit, and none of it "
"needs a release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:93 2ba9f4ef97994cda906ee120835d929a
msgid ""
"Two kinds live here, maintained differently: **ours**, written by the app"
" as well as read by it (``distances.json``, ``events.json``, "
"``categories.json``, ``notes.json``, ``communiques.json``, "
"``entry_formats.json``); and **theirs**, read-only and replaced wholesale"
" by a newer version (``penalties.json`` from the UCI, ``PUIS.json`` from "
"the federation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:103 744913aae2d64eaab7c779392b5d9cd0
msgid "File"
msgstr "File"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:104 9dc4c28784514b5488ddf09fb331c929
msgid "Read by"
msgstr "Letto da"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:105 cfd1486659ac46318425d0631f011d7a
msgid "What it holds"
msgstr "Che cosa contiene"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:106 6bf4b7d9849c49f7a2d8ea81103c55e4
msgid "``events.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:107 ../../reference/files.rst:111
#: 68eb6f30733e44979ff41dc780c146b6 db348f123e3b468c9d3d89e42e9c55b5
msgid "``core.catalogue``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:108 7866b6cb8b654a27ac8d416b27d6ac87
msgid ""
"What an event *is*: code, name per language, UCI abbreviation, format, "
"riders per team, how many start together, the entry-column headings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:110 1d555deddb494b39bb8844178b7c0548
msgid "``categories.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:112 d0fdc96b602e4eef9d9c719216817e42
msgid "The standard category codes, with sex and name per language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:113 7072d7928f6f4ea09699d01f65e361d1
msgid "``distances.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:114 a7ef8a94e0ea4b6ebdbca3994b0e53ab
msgid "``core.distances``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:115 c02690e02c924ae7894a94ced4194d9c
msgid "How long a race is, how often it sprints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:116 abf3febf365845e3b39fb84a01cc302a
msgid "``entry_formats.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:117 0ca1a5ac2dce4efeb03db7e37a70c9e4
msgid "``core.entry_formats``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:118 986eff0c0d214618be4f5fefebd69c5d
msgid "How each shape of entry file is read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:119 ef91bf96a1a846c4bcb24c0fd2dd1c4f
msgid "``notes.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:120 faa4ae7cb8ce460bac16ae9062c39ac2
msgid "``core.notes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:121 90320454d9f843bcb9a7a58a755a2bd3
msgid "Which regulation line opens which sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:122 5bb3d5fde5d04446b2fbc88e0b21ee3c
msgid "``communiques.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:123 b33ec9fa5fa142e182da662bed60a15f
msgid "``core.communiques``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:124 32600b3ed2d74fc2aebc30086002cf5f
msgid "Which sheets share a number, per format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:125 ef5b0719429e4158a9d4de8cdf21f018
msgid "``penalties.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:126 ../../reference/files.rst:130
#: 574c21b385424efc8740901d05fcabe9 8cdbf2658a4845518c92b9c8e379bef4
msgid "``core.decisions``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:127 ed9e408be61d4397ae52ba2c33b41584
msgid ""
"The UCI wording of track offences, in four languages, numbered as the UCI"
" numbers them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:129 dcd20967fa094a2d8907e803d2967103
msgid "``PUIS.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:131 07f07dfdf603439098f74ba2733f7753
msgid "The federal table of what each infringement costs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:133 fa631d376f0f4c74a7c6a1e6af487916
msgid ""
"Every file carries ``_last_updated_``, and most carry ``_about_``. "
"Neither is read by the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:136 2c145574e6464996b8aa10b27307cee5
msgid ""
"The **name of an event is per language**, because it is not a label: it "
"is written into ``programme.yaml`` and printed on the sheets exactly as "
"it stands there. Adding an event to an English competition writes the "
"English name, and it prints in English next year too, whoever opens the "
"file. An event the table does not know is still declared by hand in the "
"programme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:142 9ffe3ff1319b40f8a8b95b591c0a6359
msgid ""
"Distances are matched loosely on three levels — **event → category → "
"round**. A round is looked up by its own name first, then by the family "
"it belongs to, then by ``*``. Nothing here is invented: the file ships "
"seeded from a programme that was actually run, and an event the table "
"says nothing about proposes no distance at all — a blank field on the "
"page rather than a wrong number on a sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:148 972e4f2a661f4d47ac5e44032a8c9f79
msgid ""
"``notes.json`` holds two things. **Which line goes on which sheet** is "
"``rules``, and it ships filled in, because it is the regulation — one "
"rule per sentence, naming the format, the round, the document and the "
"condition. **The numbers are the programme's**: a rule names the field it"
" reads, and the placeholder is filled from the round as the jury typed "
"it. ``texts`` is the installation's own wording of any catalogue entry, "
"and it ships empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:159 6cde4cf825d94c1fb8e1dcef2272976b
msgid "Printing"
msgstr "Stampa"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:161 281d1969566140baadb95d8104f42988
msgid "One pipeline for every sheet the app produces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:179 a7426cbaba1d42a1a94189691048e310
msgid ""
"**``w`` is a weight, not a width.** The table normalises its columns' "
"weights to percentages summing to 100, so no sheet can starve a column "
"into a two-character sliver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:183 13c6e3b7154c429bb7ea7ae73fe45a71
msgid ""
"**``min_mm`` is the one thing a weight cannot express**: how narrow a "
"column may actually get *on paper*. A name that loses its last letters is"
" still a name; ``DNF`` truncated to ``DN…`` and a UCI ID missing two "
"digits are not the thing they are printed for. Those columns declare the "
"millimetres they need and the table gives them, out of what the others "
"were sharing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:189 f6f21680764942dd81b003e0cf1cb05a
msgid ""
"**Notes are tinted by kind.** A disqualification and \"the first two go "
"through to the final\" are both prose in a box, and they are not the same"
" thing: one is a sanction a team may appeal, the other is how the "
"tournament is run. The plain note prints last and keeps its grey, because"
" a colour on it would say somebody had been sanctioned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:195 663f5c75e86c42c3abd8780017c45d95
msgid ""
"**Landscape is opt-in, never automatic.** Chrome does not repeat a table "
"header group across the pages of a named page, so a landscape communiqué "
"loses its letterhead on every continuation sheet — the one thing these "
"documents must not lose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:200 45a7117942cc46199bc59294546a5a02
msgid ""
"The sheets carry a full-width letterhead and footer repeated on every "
"page — they are the ``thead`` and ``tfoot`` of one table, which is how a "
"browser repeats them. Around the table, six slots, each holding one of "
"``communique``, ``printed_at`` or nothing; an element lives in one place,"
" so putting it elsewhere removes it from where it was. A provisional "
"sheet (``draft=True``) prints a \"not final\" box where the number goes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:207 3d5f142c1258488ca3e5c57995189b67
msgid ""
"``render/print.css`` is one file used in two places: inlined into the "
"standalone page that Chromium prints, and injected into the Streamlit app"
" so the previews look like the sheet. Everything in it is scoped to "
"``.cmsr`` except the ``@media print`` block, which hides the sidebar and "
"the toolbar when the jury prints straight from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:215 ef2ab95742714757bc68ff2870804065
msgid ""
"The CSS goes in through ``st.markdown``, not ``st.html``: the latter "
"sanitises what it is handed and throws away its ``<style>``. The same "
"sanitiser drops the whole SVG namespace, which is why the derny charts "
"are drawn with ``st.markdown`` too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:220 7a7aeb2cfc164526ae3c975d837f560d
msgid ""
"``render/pdf.py`` runs a headless Chromium — the same engine the jury "
"would print with by hand, so the PDF is what the browser's own print "
"produces minus its date and URL header. No extra Python dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:224 48d9ec447dfe40cd923bbc420e431167
msgid ""
"**Where Chromium works is not where the document ends up.** The browser "
"has to *read* the page and *write* the PDF, and a sandboxed Chromium can "
"do neither under ``/tmp`` nor on the network mount the communiqués folder"
" usually is. So ``work_dirs`` tries the caller's directory first, then "
"local candidates, and only the finished bytes are written to the "
"destination. A directory that has worked once goes to the front — "
"printing a whole day must not pay for the same failed attempt on every "
"sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:232 f93db5ab0ada43a681cc1428e4a5689e
msgid ""
"``out_name`` produces ``018_classification_madison_final.pdf`` — the "
"communiqué number, then a slug of the title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:235 dfbd28c54d8447e8943c33fe4544ebc8
msgid ""
"``render/markup.py`` is four constructs of markdown — headings, bold, "
"italic, code, bullets, numbers, a rule, paragraphs — for the one place in"
" the app that takes prose rather than a field. **Everything is escaped "
"before anything is read.** What the jury types is text, never markup: a "
"sheet that renders an ``<img>`` somebody pasted into the box is a sheet "
"that can be made to say anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:246 5e7a4e06f20b418088751f3d40842d5c
msgid "Translations"
msgstr "Traduzioni"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:248 0ef94de5b241449489ac17d4f9186406
msgid ""
"The code speaks UCI English — competition, event, round, bib, club, "
"region. What reaches a screen or a printed sheet is a **lookup, never a "
"literal**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:260 f4237af34356485db06f4ddd478240ff
msgid ""
"Nothing under ``core/``, ``render/`` or ``ui/`` writes prose of its own. "
"Adding a language is adding one module and listing it in ``CATALOGUES``; "
"correcting a wording is editing one entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:264 9cb5e9aaa39948589664ba4b2c84944d
msgid ""
"Each catalogue defines the same dictionaries, named by what they name: "
"``FIELDS`` (a column of the entry list), ``RACE`` (a column or word of a "
"race sheet), ``DOCS`` (a kind of document), ``STATUSES`` and "
"``STATUS_NAMES`` (the result codes as printed and spelled out), "
"``PENALTIES``, ``NOTE_KINDS``, ``CODES``, ``UI``, ``HELP`` and ``MSG``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:270 398a7f201b8b41da8070a14e17622661
msgid ""
"``label(key)`` does **not** raise on an unknown key — it comes back "
"capitalised, so a new column still shows up readable. ``ui``, ``msg`` and"
" ``help_text`` do: a missing control label is a bug to fix, not a word to"
" invent. A key the language in force does not have is answered from the "
"default catalogue, which is a good deal better than an empty widget or a "
"``KeyError`` at the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:276 4b1ae138ccfc49a1b70b0ce6bced17a9
msgid ""
"The language is **per competition**, chosen in the settings and set once "
"per rerun before anything draws a word. It moves the **catalogue only**: "
"what ``programme.yaml`` spells out — the names of the categories, the "
"events and the rounds — prints as it is written there, in any language. "
"Those strings are also the keys races are stored under."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:282 b8ec4f407e434c3eb269d93920784e6b
msgid ""
"To add a language: copy an existing catalogue, translate the values "
"keeping every key, set ``NAME``, and add it to ``CATALOGUES``. "
"``tests/test_i18n.py`` then checks that every key the app asks for "
"exists, that every language answers all of them **with the same "
"placeholders**, and that no module outside ``core/i18n/`` writes prose of"
" its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:288 38dacca01e2b445fb87d335463892310
msgid ""
"The abbreviations a printed sheet uses are the **UCI** ones — see the "
":ref:`glossary`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:295 32fe8ef9f90945cda26bbc49890fb810
msgid "Packaging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:297 54dc4aa52d444de4b24a9db78b7aa0a6
msgid ""
"**Not implemented yet.** There is no installer, no release to download, "
"and no published build: the app runs from a checkout (:ref:`install`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:300 c328cc02f15743f38f34e10005c90c1c
msgid ""
"``packaging/`` holds the work in progress — a PyInstaller spec, an Inno "
"Setup script and an icon builder — and ``.github/workflows/build.yml`` "
"the CI that would drive them. None of it ships anything today, and the "
"notes on freezing Streamlit, on what the bundle weighs and on the per-"
"user install layout have been taken out of this page rather than left "
"standing as if they described something you could install. They come back"
" with the first release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:307 80d17bed828a4be28cdafa2f6a4318eb
msgid ""
"What is already true, and is not a packaging concern, is that "
"``core.paths`` keeps *what the program is* apart from *what the jury "
"made* — see :ref:`storage`. That separation is what a packaged build "
"would rely on."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Windows build"
#~ msgstr "La build per Windows"

#~ msgid "The console ships as an ``.exe`` a jury installs by double-clicking."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Out comes ``dist/BlueBand-<version>-setup.exe``. CI"
#~ " does the same on every ``v*`` "
#~ "tag and attaches it to the "
#~ "release."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "What it weighs, and why"
#~ msgstr "Quanto pesa, e perché"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The app installs at **about 435 "
#~ "MB**, and most of that is three"
#~ " packages the console never imports "
#~ "by name: pandas, numpy and pyarrow "
#~ "(~334 MB), Streamlit and its "
#~ "dependencies (~87 MB), CPython and the"
#~ " bootloader (~20 MB). The app itself,"
#~ " with its regulations and templates, "
#~ "is about 1 MB."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "They are there because ``st.dataframe`` "
#~ "and ``st.data_editor`` are made of them."
#~ " **This was measured, and the "
#~ "alternative was built and rejected**: "
#~ "hand-written HTML tables brought the "
#~ "installation down to 108 MB and "
#~ "were worse to use — rows twice "
#~ "as tall, a select too narrow to"
#~ " read, and none of the sorting, "
#~ "resizing, full screen, search and copy"
#~ " that come free. Keep that in "
#~ "mind before \"optimising\" the dependency "
#~ "list: the size is a decision that"
#~ " has already been taken, once, with"
#~ " numbers."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "The three awkward things about freezing Streamlit"
#~ msgstr "Le tre scomodità del congelare Streamlit"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "All three are solved in "
#~ "``packaging/blueband.spec``, and each was a"
#~ " build that succeeded and then failed"
#~ " at runtime:"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Streamlit reads its own version from"
#~ " its installed metadata.** Without the "
#~ "``.dist-info`` in the bundle it "
#~ "raises at import — ``copy_metadata``."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**Its frontend is data.** "
#~ "``streamlit/static/`` is the compiled React"
#~ " app — ``collect_data_files``."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "**The app is never imported.** The "
#~ "analysis starts at ``launcher.py``, which "
#~ "hands Streamlit ``app.py`` as a *path*,"
#~ " so ``core``, ``ui`` and ``render`` "
#~ "are in no import graph: the bundle"
#~ " starts, serves a page, and dies "
#~ "on ``No module named 'core'`` at "
#~ "the first render. ``collect_submodules``, with"
#~ " the repository put on ``sys.path`` "
#~ "first — without that it finds "
#~ "nothing and returns an empty list "
#~ "**with only a warning**."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "``BlueBand.exe --check`` is the guard "
#~ "against all three: it imports every "
#~ "module and looks for every data "
#~ "file, and it fails at the door "
#~ "instead of on the jury's first "
#~ "click."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The install is **per-user on "
#~ "purpose**, twice over: no administrator "
#~ "prompt on a laptop nobody has the"
#~ " password for, and the program's "
#~ "folder stays writable — Streamlit serves"
#~ " the last saved PDFs out of "
#~ "``static/`` inside it."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Building on Linux"
#~ msgstr "Costruirlo su Linux"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The whole recipe except the ``.ico`` "
#~ "and the installer works on Linux, "
#~ "and that is worth doing before "
#~ "pushing a tag:"
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Build it in a **clean virtual "
#~ "environment**, never in a working "
#~ "scientific one: PyInstaller bundles what "
#~ "it finds, and the ``excludes`` in "
#~ "the spec are a safety net rather"
#~ " than a guarantee."
#~ msgstr ""

